@startuml
title Figure 10 — UML Deployment diagram — packaged runtime and selectable R4 Stage-3 backend
top to bottom direction
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 55

node "Operator device" as Device <<device>> {
  artifact "Web browser" as Browser
}

node "Docker Compose / Linux host" as Host <<executionEnvironment>> {
  node "application service / container" as App <<executionEnvironment>> {
    node "embedded Tomcat 11" as Tomcat <<executionEnvironment>> {
      artifact "React static assets\nclasspath /static" as React
      artifact "Spring MVC /api/*" as Api
    }
    artifact "Spring Boot executable JAR\nsame artifact for each R4 variant" as Jar
    artifact "Stage-3 selection\nspecgraph.analysis.backend\ndeterministic | openai | local(reserved)" as BackendSelection
    artifact "Deterministic model adapter\ndefault / no credential" as Offline
  }

  node "database service / container\nR2+ when activated" as DB <<database>> {
    artifact "PostgreSQL + pgvector" as PostgreSQL
  }
}

node "External AI provider\noptional backend=openai only" as Provider <<external>>

Browser --> Tomcat : HTTP\nhost-published application port
Tomcat --> React : static /
Tomcat --> Api : in-process /api/*
Jar --> Tomcat : packaged runtime
Api --> DB : JDBC / PostgreSQL\nTCP 5432 private project network
Jar --> BackendSelection : typed bootstrap configuration
BackendSelection --> Offline : deterministic default
BackendSelection ..> Provider : HTTPS only when backend=openai

note bottom of Host
  R0-R3 retain their historical checkpoint ports. R4 uses the same application artifact with an
  orthogonal Stage-3 backend selection. Repeating compose.r4.yaml with distinct Compose project
  names creates isolated application/network/PostgreSQL state for side-by-side variants, e.g.
  deterministic baseline on :8084 and optional OpenAI synthesis on :8087. These are R4 execution
  variants, not new delivery rings. Provider credentials configure the OpenAI leaf but never
  select it. backend=local is reserved by the typed contract and fails closed until #251 lands.
end note
@enduml
